{"author":{"id":"1f592c0ac5a83ec8bdb9b8574bd8dddf2082ee3c98ad9608c7b89c82d05faf99"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791892534,"nonce":"5w5/p3DvCtkLAdFRvSVO/h5guF4=","title":"Tag the native RGB encoder color conversion matrix","message":"Independent FFmpeg decoding of ChimpMonk's solid red/green reference film produces red (231,0,1) and green (18,255,8), while explicitly decoding as BT.709 produces (253,0,0) and (0,254,0). VideoToolbox converts native BGRA input with BT.709 but the H.264 stream has no color_space tag, so independent players default to BT.601. Set the encoder's matrix explicitly and preserve it in H.264 SPS output. Verify raw decoded colors within 10 code values without external matrix overrides before hlavi publication.","files":null}]}